RED round 6 - CMUX_AGENT_LAUNCH_KIND promoted above the socket shape

This is the naive reading of "reconcile socket-shape detection with the official
CMUX_AGENT_LAUNCH_KIND=omo contract": treat the documented contract as the
highest-precedence signal.

	if (environment.CMUX_AGENT_LAUNCH_KIND === CMUX_OMO_LAUNCH_KIND) return true
	const tmuxEnvironment = environment.TMUX
	...

$ bun test packages/tmux-core/src/cmux-detect.test.ts

-   "socket=true  kind=omo tmux=real   -> false",
+   "socket=true  kind=omo tmux=real   -> true",
-   "socket=false kind=omo tmux=absent -> false",
+   "socket=false kind=omo tmux=absent -> true",
-   "socket=false kind=omo tmux=real   -> false",
+   "socket=false kind=omo tmux=real   -> true",
(fail) #given every combination of both cmux signals and a TMUX shape
(fail) #given a real tmux socket inherited alongside both cmux signals
       #then the socket shape outranks both signals
(fail) #given only CMUX_AGENT_LAUNCH_KIND with no socket path and no TMUX
       #then returns false (fails closed on an inherited-only signal)

 12 pass
 3 fail

Two of the three failures are the nested-real-tmux invariant this review asked to
preserve, and the third is the fail-closed boundary. The cause is measured, not
assumed: CMUX_AGENT_LAUNCH_KIND is inherited by a real tmux server started inside
a cmux pane (see live-signal-inheritance.log), so it describes the launcher, not
the socket we would actually talk to. That is why the shipped algorithm keeps the
launch kind subordinate to the TMUX socket shape.
